.TH SONORA-RIP 1 "2026" "sonora-rip 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sonora-rip \- Audio CD / SACD ripper with automatic pre-emphasis correction
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sonora-rip cd
[\fB\-d\fR DEV] [\fB\-o\fR DIR] [\fB\-t\fR N[-M]] [\fB\-\-deemph\fR auto|on|off] [\fB\-\-format\fR wav|flac] [\fB\-\-flac\-level\fR 0-8] [\fB\-\-dither\fR] [\fB\-\-fast\fR]
.br
.B sonora-rip sacd \-i
ISO|DEV|HOST[:2002] [\fB\-o\fR DIR] [\fB\-\-multichannel\fR] [\fB\-\-pcm\fR [\fB\-\-rate\fR HZ] [\fB\-\-bits\fR 16|24]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
In CD mode each track's Red Book pre-emphasis flag is read; flagged tracks are
passed through a 50/15 microsecond de-emphasis filter before being written as WAV.
In SACD mode the external sacd_extract tool reads the disc/ISO and produces DSF
files, optionally converted to PCM with ffmpeg.
.SH FLAC
With \fB\-\-format flac\fR, CD tracks are encoded losslessly with libFLAC (verification enabled) and tagged with TRACKNUMBER, ENCODER and the pre-emphasis flag / de-emphasis status.
.SH CDDB
In CD mode the disc is looked up on gnudb.gnudb.org (CDDBP port 8880) unless
\fB\-\-no\-cddb\fR is given. \fB\-\-cddb\-server\fR HOST[:PORT] selects another
server, \fB\-\-cddb\-http\fR uses HTTP (port 80) and \fB\-\-cddb\-match\fR N picks
the N-th candidate. Results fill ARTIST, ALBUM, ALBUMARTIST, TITLE, DATE, GENRE,
TRACKTOTAL and CDDB_DISCID tags (FLAC) and the names: files are written to OUTDIR/"Artist - Album"/NN-Title.ext.
.SH LICENSE
GPL-2.0-or-later.
